Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this Next.js project.

## Changes Made

### Installation
- Installed `@vercel/analytics` package (version 2.0.1) using npm
- Updated package.json and package-lock.json with the new dependency

### Configuration
- Modified `app/layout.tsx` to integrate Vercel Web Analytics:
  - Added import statement: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next";`
  - Added `<Analytics />` component at the end of the body element in the root layout

### Implementation Details
- Followed the official Vercel documentation (https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart)
- Used the App Router configuration method (as this project uses Next.js App Router)
- Placed the Analytics component in the root layout to track all pages automatically
- The Analytics component is added after the children to ensure proper page loading

### Verification
- ✅ Build completed successfully with no errors
- ✅ Linter passed with no warnings or errors
- ✅ TypeScript compilation successful
- ✅ All static pages generated correctly

### Next Steps
To enable analytics in production:
1. Deploy the application to Vercel
2. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel dashboard under the Analytics tab
3. Analytics will automatically start tracking page views and interactions

The implementation is complete and ready for deployment.
